From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 06:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH v2] nl80211: match a cold-started shared-wiphy BSS by its BSSID
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Build-20 lane d aborts once per boot inside the F108 window (run-47d,
d01 a03-full-logread.txt:8448, d02 :8625):

  wld: hapdRad - [x]wlan0: bss wlan0.3 (wlan0.3) is held by iface of
  unknown bss wlan0.1, abort radio removal
  wld: genFsm  - [x]wlan0: warm apply failed to remove iface conf =>
  restart to recover

F108 sets Radio.*.RegulatoryDomain=DE, which makes pWHM restart the
hostapd process cold with the three radio config files. The new ifaces
enter COUNTRY_UPDATE and stay there: setup_interface() (src/ap/hostapd.c
in the hostapd tree) sees a previous country different from the new one
and waits up to 5 s for the channel list update. Two seconds later F108
sets Radio.3.PowerType=VeryLowPower on the same 6 GHz radio (wlan0),
whose FSM commit then runs GEN_FSM_REMOVE_HOSTAPD to rewrite its iface
config, and wld_rad_hostapd_removeConf() takes its socket snapshot in
that window.

What hostapd exposes there: start_ctrl_iface() has already published
every BSS socket; STATUS reports state=COUNTRY_UPDATE, phy=<wiphy name>
(a cold start carries no ADD label) and freq=0, since iface->freq is
only set by setup_interface2(). bss[0] already has its nonzero own_addr
from i802_init(), the secondary BSSes keep 00:00:00:00:00:00 until
hostapd_setup_bss() runs after the country update.

wld_hostapd_resolveSock() classifies wlan0.2/wlan0.3 as initializing
(zero BSSID in COUNTRY_UPDATE, 0022). For wlan0.1 it never compares the
BSSID: s_radioMatches() rejects every Radio because phy is the shared
wiphy name, no frequency is available and the multi_radio=1 hwsim wiphy
hosts three Radios (0001). With zero candidate Radios the socket ends
"unknown or ambiguous AP" and unresolved. removeConf() then finds the
initializing local wlan0.3 held by that unresolved owner and aborts
before the 0022 retry can return NOT_AVAILABLE, so the FSM falls back
to a full process restart. Real boards, with one Radio per wiphy, pass
the same predicate and resolve the same socket.

Let a self-listed BSS with a nonzero BSSID, the shared physical wiphy
name and no usable frequency reach the BSSID comparison against every
Radio of that wiphy in the same control directory. Such a candidate has
no radio evidence of its own, so s_matchAP() does not apply its
current-first policy to it: the BSSID must be the current identity of
exactly one candidate AP and the remembered identity of none, over all
candidate Radios. A remembered identity alone, or one current match
next to an AP that still remembers the same address (reused address
with the previous configuration still loaded), stays unresolved. A
logical Radio label or a usable frequency keeps the strict predicate
and its policy, and zero-BSSID sockets keep their 0022 classification.
The removal owner guard is unchanged; wld_hostapd_mayBelongToRadio() is
not widened, it already compares the BSSID against the Radio's own APs.
With wlan0.1 resolved the snapshot returns NOT_AVAILABLE for the
initializing secondaries and s_tryRemoveHostapd() retries within its
bounded budget instead of restarting hostapd.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_sock.c | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_sock.c b/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_sock.c
index e7bb41948fda..ee5ba7271d75 100644
--- a/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_sock.c
+++ b/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_sock.c
@@ -126,6 +126,26 @@ static bool s_radioMatches(const wld_hostapd_sock_t* pSock, T_Radio* pRad) {
            (label || pSock->hasBand || (wld_rad_countWiphyRads(pRad->wiphy) == 1));
 }
 
+/*
+ * A cold-started hostapd iface reports the physical wiphy name and no
+ * frequency until setup_interface2() runs (COUNTRY_UPDATE, channel list
+ * wait). On a wiphy shared by several Radios that evidence identifies no
+ * single Radio, but the first BSS already carries its driver-initialized
+ * nonzero BSSID. Let such a BSS reach the BSSID comparison against every
+ * Radio of that wiphy. Without positive radio evidence s_matchAP() then
+ * accepts only a BSSID that exactly one candidate AP holds as its current
+ * identity and none holds as a remembered one; anything else stays
+ * unresolved. A logical Radio label or a usable frequency keeps the
+ * strict predicate above and its current-first policy.
+ * wld_hostapd_mayBelongToRadio() is not widened: it already compares the
+ * BSSID against the Radio's own APs.
+ */
+static bool s_sharedWiphyCandidate(const wld_hostapd_sock_t* pSock, T_Radio* pRad) {
+    return !pSock->hasBand && !swl_mac_binIsNull(&pSock->bssid) &&
+           swl_str_matches(pSock->phy, pRad->wiphyName) &&
+           (wld_rad_countWiphyRads(pRad->wiphy) > 1);
+}
+
 /* Re-evaluate current/remembered BSSIDs on every hit; retain no AP pointers. */
 static swl_rc_ne s_matchAP(const char* dir, wld_hostapd_sock_t* pSock) {
     pSock->ap = NULL;
@@ -133,12 +153,18 @@ static swl_rc_ne s_matchAP(const char* dir, wld_hostapd_sock_t* pSock) {
     T_AccessPoint* pCurrent = NULL;
     T_AccessPoint* pOld = NULL;
     unsigned int currentCount = 0, oldCount = 0;
+    bool fallback = false;
     T_Radio* pRad = NULL;
     wld_for_eachRad(pRad) {
-        if((pRad->hostapd == NULL) || !s_radioMatches(pSock, pRad) ||
+        if(pRad->hostapd == NULL) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        bool strict = s_radioMatches(pSock, pRad);
+        if((!strict && !s_sharedWiphyCandidate(pSock, pRad)) ||
            !swl_str_matches(dir, wld_wpaCtrlMngr_getCtrlIfaceDirPath(wld_secDmn_getWpaCtrlMgr(pRad->hostapd)))) {
             continue;
         }
+        fallback |= !strict;
         T_AccessPoint* pAP = NULL;
         wld_rad_forEachAp(pAP, pRad) {
             if((pAP->pSSID == NULL) || (pAP->wpaCtrlInterface == NULL)) {
@@ -155,6 +181,13 @@ static swl_rc_ne s_matchAP(const char* dir, wld_hostapd_sock_t* pSock) {
     }
     ASSERTI_TRUE((currentCount == 1) || ((currentCount == 0) && (oldCount == 1)),
                  SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "unknown or ambiguous AP: %s", pSock->name);
+    /* A shared-wiphy candidate has no radio evidence of its own, so neither
+     * a current match over a remembered one nor a remembered identity alone
+     * may pick an AP across Radios: the BSSID must be unique over the union
+     * of current and remembered identities of every candidate AP.
+     */
+    ASSERTI_FALSE(fallback && ((currentCount != 1) || (oldCount != 0)),
+                  SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "shared-wiphy BSSID is not unique: %s", pSock->name);
     pSock->ap = currentCount ? pCurrent : pOld;
     pSock->resolved = true;
     return SWL_RC_OK;
